# v0.25.4 — Bridge, escrow/consensus hardening, GPU electricity-cost floor, repo-wide cleanup

**Baseline**: end of `v0.25.3` coverage at `47401ce757` (2026-08-31); `v0.25.3` was documented but never tagged.
**Date**: 2026-09-06.
**Tag**: `v0.25.4` (pending).

This release covers the 300 commits between the end of the `v0.25.3` change log and `main` (`a47ae3715`). Headline items: the hub-only two-way ETH-AITBC bridge with live Sepolia validation, escrow and payment settlement hardening, a GPU electricity-cost floor for fixed-duration rentals with EVM and native parity, PBFT/multi-validator consensus fixes including gossip mesh and proposer-schedule signature checks, RPC API-key enforcement, secret migration to `blockchain-secrets.env`, contract test-suite repair with fuzz coverage, and a large dead-code/stale-docs cleanup.

## Changes

### Two-way ETH-AITBC bridge (hub-only)

- `feat(bridge)`: hub-only two-way ETH-AITBC bridge (`6f405b3707`), with live Sepolia round-trip fixes (`dd988df7f0`).
- Bridge tests: `BRIDGE_WITHDRAW`, DB, reserve guard, and refund tests (`374e1740a3`).
- Money stored as `Decimal`; MCP server synced with the ETH-AIT bridge (`2c27299d0d`).
- Bridge reliability: init target chain DB before probing/backfilling bridge validators (`128a68d8d0`, `d9ba6a7d55`), backfill validators for supported chains (`a645839e72`), do not mark a transfer completed until the release tx is block-sealed (`cf8777f34f`), derive `bridge_state_root` on P2P-synced blocks (`33d9a26ebb`), retry transient ETH RPC connection failures in wallet-bridge (`1441a98bd3`).

### Escrow and payments

- `X-API-Key` auth on escrow endpoints; reinvest address derived from contract (`20dcbfdb19`); marketplace sends `X-API-Key` when creating escrows (`a1d1a1a286`); CLI passes `BLOCKCHAIN_RPC_API_KEY` to escrow RPC (`5b1e699321`); `BlockchainRPCClient` falls back to `BLOCKCHAIN_RPC_API_KEY` env (`1613abf3e3`).
- `get_escrow` derives state from timestamps with status fallback (`e02f4fc8bb`); guard refund/release against stale status (`035c56418d`); guard refund after job completion, fix micro rounding, harden release idempotency (`ba452d446d`).
- Persist `release_tx_hash` and reject release without it (`dd9805e4a0`); backfill `release_tx_hash` on replay and commit the backfill (`442692da3b`, `1c5bf331ad`).
- Validate `auto_reinvest_address` against the escrow provider in `_auto_stake` (`a0a492717e`).
- Stop direct `POST /register-account` calls; create recipients in block state (`e6487d957b`); ensure provider account exists in the `ESCROW_LOCK` transition (`10c401aa55`).
- `ESCROW_LOCK` fee is 1% with a dust floor (`60189e2e96`); bill the requested amount and return the buyer change (`ca51ae19bb`); the escrowed principal is the lock, not lock plus fee (`7f47b68e99`); settlement legs read from the chain, not the last txn (`385bd8a933`); node wallet advertised on `/health` so clients lock against it (`7e73818fe2`).
- Stuck-escrow sweeper hardened with an on-chain hash invariant; refund semantics documented (`0718134613`).
- Escrow-release retries bounded with a `settlement_failed` terminal state (`ff89c1a7e2`).
- `ipfs_rental_sweeper` uses `rental_id` as `job_id` for escrow release/refund (`1a00e273e9`).
- CLI paid submits abort when the provider is missing or the escrow is left unsecured (`4eee07d529`, `efe9ba8fb6`).

### Consensus (PBFT / multi-validator PoA)

- Block producers may start in multi-validator mode regardless of `blockchain_mode` (`7a5d6216c5`); proposer key/id required before starting the multi-validator producer (`684aac701d`); block production defaults to all supported chains and loads the validator set for status (`76be7d5988`).
- `multi_validator_min_attestations` honored for PBFT quorum during rollout (`c209719a71`); status endpoint reports PBFT `required_messages` accordingly (`5d200224d2`); PBFT/attestation quorum made dynamic and `MultiValidatorPoA.validate_block` wired in (`90fd018b71`); multi-validator attestation gate fixed in `poa.py` (`e549a19c40`).
- PBFT round audit logging and structured timeout diagnostics (`b4f4678286`); a later round may supersede one that produced no block (`d3861a2ebf`); the proposer rotates when the scheduled one is unavailable (`cb8cfbf25e`); proposer-schedule validation skipped for unknown proposers during import (`379992d7db`); heartbeat idle time uses the chain head timestamp (`c786fc7ab3`, `e670ca8fed`).
- Transaction records kept out of per-tx nested savepoints (`3acefcda7d`); account rows no longer leak from rejected transactions (`ad2981f9e0`) and are no longer written outside consensus (`d639db7ba1`); staking and bounty balances moved into block processing (`268307b8e6`); HTLC swap settlement deferred to block processing (`4151dfee84`).
- Signed state roots carried into the follower's proposer-schedule check (`430d11ab74`); state/bridge roots carried through the proposer-signature check (`ba01001d03`) — this is the `bridge_state_root` bug that made node1 reject signed block 2555 mid-rollout.
- Local state divergence is now told apart from a bad block (`a05962ebf4`).
- State-transition version gate for historical replay (`b6f43f6eb7`); deterministic block-version threshold tests (`4fea041f4d`).
- Tests: PBFT fault tolerance with one down validator (`63f271d2d7`), majority/minority partition tests (`cd874ca5e3`), bulk-fork coverage (`3dec6c4d44`).

### Gossip / P2P

- New mesh backend so validators gossip peer-to-peer instead of via the hub (`3a18de6ea9`); authenticated validator gossip and secure open-island onboarding (`10d2c2d902`).
- Restricted-topic matching corrected for `pbft`, `consensus`, and blocks (`8bd814d97e`, `a2b2fb2bc5`); topic-matching regression tests and explicit client-IP extraction (`f3e0d3816e`); per-IP limit key derived from `X-Forwarded-For`/`X-Real-IP` (`c99aa5a8aa`); per-IP connection and rate limits raised (`7a878e21ac`).
- Attestation responses sharing a block hash are no longer deduplicated away (`9ac10c792c`).
- `broker.py` split into a `backends` package (`a620e13344`).
- Redis credentials redacted from service logs and gossip logs (`918792dd42`, `7a878e21ac`); `GOSSIP_BROADCAST_URL` read from env in broadcast tests (`ab31e3700a`) and loaded from `blockchain.env`/`node.env` for trading (`bc68b8fc0c`).

