### GPU electricity-cost floor for fixed-duration rentals

- Shared energy quote and floor arithmetic (`c8a271b7b`): `aitbc/marketplace/energy_pricing.py` introduces `EnergyQuote`, `EnergyProfile`, `EnergyRate`, deterministic quote serialization/digesting, `quote_energy_floor()`, and `evaluate_quote()` so a fixed-duration GPU rental freezes its economic terms at funding.
- Native and EVM paths treated as separate enforcement systems. Native gates are in service paths; no consensus rule changes.
- EVM contracts updated (`c8a271b7b`): `IEnergyPricing` interface, `DynamicPricing` energy profile/rate functions, `AIPowerRental` protected funding and `startRental` gating, and `EscrowService` protected compute-escrow gates (`c8a271b7b`). Solidity tests added in `contracts/test/fuzz/AIPowerRental.t.sol`, `contracts/test/fuzz/EscrowService.t.sol`, and `contracts/test/fuzz/DynamicPricingEnergy.t.sol`.
- Solidity getter fixes (`0c6d11767`, `50b40995d`, `d9060c599`): struct view functions `getRentalEnergyTerms()` and `getComputeEscrowTerms()` added to avoid auto-generated public-mapping tuple returns; enum casts and struct field access fixed in tests.
- Coordinator payment gate (`c8a271b7b`, `1d2a63b74`): protected payment creation requires an energy quote, binds buyer/provider/resource/model/GPU count/duration, runs `evaluate_quote`, and persists the exact buyer charge, provider credit, fee, and net floor in `job_payments.meta_data`. The canonical `ESCROW_LOCK` transaction carries the quote ID and digest.
- Coordinator GPU marketplace (`c8a271b7b`, `1d2a63b74`): `POST /marketplace/gpu/quote` prepares a bound job and unsigned quote; `POST /marketplace/gpu/purchase` funds the prepared job with the same quote; failure rolls back the booking, GPU availability, and unstarted job.
- Blockchain-node escrow gate (`c8a271b7b`, `a156e44b7`): `Escrow` stores frozen `protected`, `energy_quote_snapshot`, `energy_quote_id`, `energy_net_floor_units`, `energy_provider_credit_units`, and `energy_fee_basis_points`. `POST /rpc/escrow/create` validates the quote and exact lock amount; protected release enforces the frozen floor and refuses arbitrary metered overrides. Under-funded releases are refused with an explicit floor message.
- Migrations (`c8a271b7b`): `f53990f9d6cc_add_energy_floor_quote_columns.py` for the coordinator `job`, `gpu_registry`, and `gpu_bookings` tables; `ec9a04333809_add_energy_floor_escrow.py` for the blockchain-node `escrow` table. Existing rows backfilled as `protected = false`.
- Type and lint fixes (`1d2a63b74`, `50b40995d`, `d9060c599`, `a47ae3715`): `dict[str, Any]` for payment/release JSON payloads, mypy narrowing for `Decimal.as_tuple().exponent`, and regenerated `docs/api/coordinator-api-openapi.json`.

## Validation

- Live Sepolia round-trip validated for the two-way bridge (deposit + withdraw paths, `dd988df7f0` family).
- PBFT mesh and proposer-schedule signature checks exercised on the live fleet; the block-2555 rejection on node1 was traced to the pre-fix `bridge_state_root` rebuild and has not recurred since fleet convergence.
- `python -m py_compile` + `ruff` clean on all files touched by the dead-stub cleanup; contract suites (forge + Hardhat) run in CI.

